  "src": "the solid teal rectangular object",
  "path": "cast horizontal rays from each source row and vertical rays from each source column; stop at a blue object or the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "paint every crossed non-blue, non-teal pixel yellow",
  "transform": "preserve the teal source and blue blockers; leave all off-ray pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 19 rows x 18-19 cols, background black (0)
  source:
    color: 8 (teal), solid rectangle, 4-7 rows x 4-7 cols
    position: roughly upper-center, gaps to all edges >= 4
    not touching any grid edge
  blockers:
    color: 1 (blue), solid rectangles, 2-8 rows x 2-9 cols
    count: 1-4 per grid
    placement: each blocker overlaps the source's row-band or col-band (but not both) so it blocks horizontal or vertical rays; 16/17 blockers are in a ray path [observed]
    partial coverage: a blocker typically covers 14-100% of the source rows/cols it faces
  passthrough_objects:
    color: 2 (red), solid rectangles, 2-6 rows x 2-13 cols
    count: 2-6 per grid; some lie in ray paths, some do not
    rays paint through them (red cells in ray path become yellow)
  colors_used: exactly {0, 1, 2, 8} in input; 4 (yellow) appears only in output
  constraints:
    - no two objects (src/blocker/passthrough) overlap; min gap >= 1 cell
    - objects may touch grid edges (blockers and passthrough often do)
    - yellow (4) absent from input
  output_rule: |
    From each source row, cast horizontal rays left & right; from each source col, cast vertical rays up & down.
    Rays paint non-source, non-blue cells yellow (4). A ray stops before any blue (1) cell or at the grid edge.
    Source and blockers are unchanged; red cells in ray paths become yellow.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (ray-casting output is deterministic from input; no inverse needed)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid 19 rows x 18-19 cols.
    2. Place source (8) rectangle 4-7 x 4-7, centered roughly upper-center with >= 4 gap to all edges.
    3. Place 1-4 blue blockers as solid rectangles. Each must overlap the source's row-band XOR col-band so it actually blocks rays. Vary coverage (partial).
    4. Place 2-6 red passthrough rectangles scattered around the grid. Some should lie in ray paths (overlapping source row/col bands) so they get painted yellow. Ensure no object overlaps.
    5. Verify no two objects overlap (gap >= 1) and yellow (4) is absent.
```
